Condition : 21 - No Phase 2 development shall commence until a detailed scheme of on-site sustainability covering:

a) measures for the harvesting of rainwater and the minimisation of water run-off,
aiming for greenfield levels;
b) grey water reuse as appropriate;
c) the sourcing of materials to be used in the construction and fitting out (involving
reuse, recycling and other sustainable sourcing);
d) the use of passive ventilation.
The scheme as approved shall be implemented prior to occupation of the Phase 2 buildings, unless otherwise approved in writing by the Local Planning
Authority, and retained thereafter. Development in Phase 1 shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and the approved details for Phase 1 (Phase 1 details approved on 20 December 2010 with reference 00657/P/P13 (21)) or as otherwise agreed in writing with the Local Authority, unless superseded by details submitted pursuant to Phase 2 and approved by the Local Planning Authority. 

Phase 1 Approved details:

St George West London Kew Bridge Road Development BREEAM Retail (2008): Design Stage Pre-Assessment Report dated 11 November version 2.0, received 11 November 2010; 

Kew Bridge Road - Response to GLA (L-R-4479-ES-002 v2) dated 30 June 2009, received 4 August 2010; 

DSSR Report - St George West London Kew - Kew Bridge Road Development: Pre-assessment Report for Domestic Dwellings for Code Level 3 (L-R-4479-CSH-001, version 2.0), dated 28 June 2010, received 4 August 2010

DSSR Report - St George West London - Kew Bridge Road, Brentford: Energy Implementation Strategy (L-R-4479-ES-003 v3, version 2.0), dated 24 June, received 4 August 2010 (as amended)

Biomass Boiler additional details received by email 10 November 2010 from St George West London.

Condition : 44 - Prior to the commencement of the Phase 2 development an Ecological
Enhancement Scheme for the provision and management of the buffer zone alongside the River Thames and the provision of biodiversity habitat for the whole site shall be submitted to and agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority. Thereafter the development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved scheme and any subsequent amendments shall be agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority.
The scheme shall include:
i) plans showing the extent and layout of the buffer zone;
ii) details of the planting scheme (this should incorporate native species where ever possible) and all species within the 16m buffer zone will need to be native;
iii) details demonstrating how the buffer zone will be protected during development and managed/maintained over the longer term;
iv) details of any footpaths, fencing, lighting etc within the buffer zone. Light spillage over the River Thames and adjacent river corridor habitat will need to be minimised using focussed lighting and cowlings, to reduce the adverse impact on species such as bats which rely on the river corridor for foraging and commuting;
v) details of green and brown roofs on the buildings. These are of particular important adjacent to river corridor due to the species they support;
vi) details of bird and bat boxes and bricks within the site;
vii) details regarding proposed in river enhancements such as timber fenders.
